2026-07-31T04:26:35.1543047Z         "github_event_payload": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1543421Z           "after": "75bce7d33d242cef76a390d2dfb398e76b7fea2b",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1543780Z           "base_ref": null,
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1544246Z           "before": "5f0802beeb402503cc257d552100de7707ed3651",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1544564Z           "commits": [
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1544772Z             {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1544971Z               "author": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1545208Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1545515Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1545763Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1545986Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1546199Z               "committer": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1546454Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1546732Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1546970Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1547669Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1547904Z               "distinct": false,
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1548206Z               "id": "73bacb2ef8ae32123e9d802c7564596e28320b7c",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1554289Z               "message": "Target net10.0 and move every package onto its current release\n\n.NET 8 reaches end of support on 10 November 2026, so the runtime had to move\nbefore then; .NET 10 is the LTS that replaces it, supported to November 2028.\n\nThe five project files retarget together, since a solution cannot straddle two\ntarget frameworks without multi-targeting every library. A global.json pins the\nSDK feature band so CI, a dev box and the container agree on which SDK builds\nthis, and the Dockerfile copies it in for the same reason — otherwise the image\nsilently builds on whatever band its base tag happens to ship.\n\nTwo package references are deleted rather than bumped. System.Text.Json was\npinned at 10.0.5 to pull a newer serializer than net8.0 carried; on net10.0 it\nis in the shared framework, where an explicit reference can only pin something\nolder than the runtime's own. Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Console is likewise\npart of Microsoft.AspNetCore.App, so the console formatter run-web.sh selects is\navailable without it.\n\nThe .claude session-start hook installed dotnet-sdk-8.0 and gated on a version\nstarting \"8.\" — left alone, every Claude Code web session would come up with an\nSDK that cannot build the repository it was opened for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016pbZnikthqk94Ai5MCCxbT",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1559782Z               "timestamp": "2026-07-30T05:40:32Z",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1560153Z               "tree_id": "2cd75da8a2d4b9ec9073fb073a855c929465690f",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1560693Z               "url": "https://github.com/pkinerd/ednsv/commit/73bacb2ef8ae32123e9d802c7564596e28320b7c"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1561162Z             },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1561360Z             {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1561544Z               "author": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1561802Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1562079Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1562332Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1562589Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1562800Z               "committer": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1563056Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1563340Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1563584Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1563808Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1564019Z               "distinct": false,
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1564312Z               "id": "03df1b2640d4d566eb5eee82b3df56f14eccf8cc",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1571715Z               "message": "Move the CLI onto the released System.CommandLine API\n\nThe CLI was on 2.0.0-beta4, whose parser API was reshaped before 2.0 shipped.\nMost of the change is mechanical — AddAlias became Aliases, a default-value\nlambda became DefaultValueFactory, GetValueForOption became GetValue,\nFindResultFor became GetResult, and invocation now goes through the ParseResult\nrather than the command.\n\nOne part is not mechanical, and is why every one of the 31 declarations is\nrewritten rather than the six that failed to compile. Option<T> now takes a name\nfollowed by aliases, so `new Option<bool>(\"--axfr\", \"Enable zone transfer…\")`\nstill builds, but registers that whole sentence as an alias and leaves the\noption with no description. It is the one API break in this migration that the\ncompiler cannot see.\n\nSetHandler bound at most eight options as lambda parameters, so the remaining\ntwenty-odd were read by parsing args a second time inside the handler. SetAction\nreceives the ParseResult, so that second parse and the comment apologising for\nit are both gone and every option is now read the same way.\n\nVerified against the pre-upgrade binary: --help is byte-identical but for\nSpectre-independent cosmetics (System.CommandLine no longer prints \"[default:\nTrue]\" for a boolean flag, and orders --version after --help), all 36 option and\nalias spellings still parse, and a full run over example.com returns the same\n35 pass / 4 warning verdict across all 87 checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016pbZnikthqk94Ai5MCCxbT",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1579014Z               "timestamp": "2026-07-30T05:40:45Z",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1579351Z               "tree_id": "226e0b9061ea76e4618e2e1b343f3b016edaa726",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1579848Z               "url": "https://github.com/pkinerd/ednsv/commit/03df1b2640d4d566eb5eee82b3df56f14eccf8cc"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1580282Z             },
