2026-07-31T04:26:35.1583033Z               "distinct": false,
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1583307Z               "id": "7a9464f2118c37da3feab54bd5941e8cbc90cb13",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1589522Z               "message": "Carry the Swagger security requirement across the OpenAPI 2.x break\n\nSwashbuckle 10 is the first release that runs on .NET 10, and it brings\nMicrosoft.OpenApi 2.x, which moved the model types out of the .Models namespace\nand removed OpenApiSecurityScheme.Reference. A reference to a named scheme is\nnow its own type, and AddSecurityRequirement takes a factory so the reference\nhas a document to resolve against.\n\nThe failure mode if this is got wrong is quiet: inlining a fresh scheme instead\nof referencing the registered \"Bearer\" definition compiles and produces a\ndocument that still validates, but Swagger UI stops attaching the Authorization\nheader and every \"Try it out\" comes back 401. Checked by diffing the generated\ndocument against the pre-upgrade build — same 23 paths, same operations, same\nschemas, and the global security block still reads [{\"Bearer\": []}]. The only\nchange is the emitted spec revision, 3.0.1 to 3.0.4.\n\nAddEndpointsApiExplorer stays. It is redundant for ASP.NET Core's own AddOpenApi\nfrom .NET 9 on, but Swashbuckle's generator is built on ApiExplorer, and dropping\nit leaves SwaggerGenerator with no constructible dependency — the container fails\nvalidation at startup and every endpoint goes down with it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016pbZnikthqk94Ai5MCCxbT",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1597755Z               "timestamp": "2026-07-30T05:41:01Z",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1598346Z               "tree_id": "8973f626e3e3d41d250f0118acfcedc8636b707a",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1599250Z               "url": "https://github.com/pkinerd/ednsv/commit/7a9464f2118c37da3feab54bd5941e8cbc90cb13"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1600294Z             },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1600603Z             {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1600915Z               "author": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1601330Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1601816Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1602232Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1602639Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1602970Z               "committer": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1603406Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1603885Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1604295Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1604708Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1605042Z               "distinct": false,
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1605526Z               "id": "03c71c8a26e08dc1ef8db08716327142f4b0dd28",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1613168Z               "message": "Disambiguate the call sites Redis 3.x and the xUnit analyzer flagged\n\nStackExchange.Redis 3.0 is an IO-core rewrite that keeps the API, but two new\noverloads change what an existing call binds to. A three-argument StringSetAsync\nnow resolves to the overload taking the library's own Expiration type, which has\nno conversion from TimeSpan?, and RedisValue converts implicitly to both string\nand a byte span, leaving JsonSerializer.Deserialize ambiguous. Both are pinned\nback to what they resolved to before — When.Always was the old default, and the\nstring overload is what the JSON payload was already going through.\n\nThe two Assert.Single calls are the xUnit 2.9 analyzer's point: filtering with\nWhere first means a failure reports \"the sequence had 2 elements\" instead of\nnaming the predicate that did not match once.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016pbZnikthqk94Ai5MCCxbT",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1619284Z               "timestamp": "2026-07-30T05:41:01Z",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1619909Z               "tree_id": "5d420396e1fd0f0590efa90080bb60f512c75b44",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1620780Z               "url": "https://github.com/pkinerd/ednsv/commit/03c71c8a26e08dc1ef8db08716327142f4b0dd28"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1621528Z             },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1621821Z             {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1622131Z               "author": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1622541Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1623018Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1623424Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1623811Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1624112Z               "committer": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1624500Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1624943Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1625328Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1625726Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1626047Z               "distinct": false,
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1626519Z               "id": "c26f279576161c5df45c8e880a1b05ff19e6a6b0",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1632513Z               "message": "Load certificates through the APIs that replaced the obsolete constructor\n\nX509Certificate2(byte[]) is obsolete from .NET 9: it sniffed the encoding, and\nguessing at a certificate's format from its bytes is what the replacement APIs\nexist to stop. The three SMTP call sites all hold DER — RawData, or base64 of\nit, read back out of the probe cache — so they take X509CertificateLoader.\n\nThe BIMI one does not. It holds the text of a PEM block, which the loader does\nnot read, so it takes CreateFromPem instead. Sending those bytes to the loader\nwould have compiled and then failed on every VMC.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016pbZnikthqk94Ai5MCCxbT",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1638806Z               "timestamp": "2026-07-30T05:41:14Z",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1639370Z               "tree_id": "8a4dd536c070f9642c49966a8865f81252ab373d",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1640074Z               "url": "https://github.com/pkinerd/ednsv/commit/c26f279576161c5df45c8e880a1b05ff19e6a6b0"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1640771Z             },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1640955Z             {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1641142Z               "author": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1641408Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1641691Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1641925Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1642154Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1642341Z               "committer": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1642589Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1642859Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1643084Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1643339Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1643527Z               "distinct": false,
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1643803Z               "id": "7f5444cf1951552f3aa769a0e9c5e565630439ab",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1647857Z               "message": "Update the docs and the one comment the runtime bump made untrue\n\nThe version table in the architecture doc listed pinned package versions, so it\ngoes stale with the upgrade rather than merely reading oddly; StackExchange.Redis\nwas missing from it and is added while the table is being corrected.\n\nProbeCache's key index was explained as a workaround for MemoryCache not being\nenumerable on .NET 8, and both the comment and the caching doc said so.\nMemoryCache has exposed Keys since .NET 9, so that reason has expired — but the\nindex is not removable, because republishing an entry into the shared tier needs\nthe expiry it is holding and Keys yields keys alone. Both places now say what\nactually keeps it there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016pbZnikthqk94Ai5MCCxbT",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1650883Z               "timestamp": "2026-07-30T05:41:14Z",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1651219Z               "tree_id": "880a0c4504c4ecff4d5fd3456ae9fbcd18254f25",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1651743Z               "url": "https://github.com/pkinerd/ednsv/commit/7f5444cf1951552f3aa769a0e9c5e565630439ab"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1652181Z             },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1652356Z             {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1652537Z               "author": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1652775Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1653049Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1653283Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1653510Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1653702Z               "committer": {
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1653943Z                 "email": "noreply@anthropic.com",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1654209Z                 "name": "Claude",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1654440Z                 "username": "claude"
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1654663Z               },
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1654848Z               "distinct": false,
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1655122Z               "id": "fe15866e031609bd970c2266799ab8e98dd21c18",
2026-07-31T04:26:35.1661418Z               "message": "Give a session the setup and the context it needs to work here\n\nThe session-start hook installed the SDK and stopped, which left the Redis-backed\ntests self-skipping in every web session — 52 of them on this commit, all logging\nthat they skipped, all counted as a pass. That is the same silent hole the CI\nworkflow grew a service container to close, so the hook now provisions a server\non 6380 the same way. It stays best-effort: running without Redis is supported,\nso nothing here may fail a session opened only to read code.\n\nThe SDK check is left keyed on \"10.\" rather than made into a comparison, because\nwith global.json pinning the band an older SDK makes `dotnet --version` fail\nrather than report an older number — a .NET 8 box therefore takes the install\npath exactly as an empty one does. That is worth a comment, since it looks like\na bug otherwise.\n\nCLAUDE.md is new. It carries the things this repository will not tell you until\nthey have already cost you an hour: that a bare `dotnet test` under-reports, that\nthe web service deliberately refuses to start network-exposed without auth, that\nSpectre.Console renders nothing when stdout is not a terminal, that CI parses\nthe CLI's summary table with a regex, and that images carry provenance rather\nthan versions. Architecture stays in docs/ where it was.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016pbZnikthqk94Ai5MCCxbT",
